VALUES (645, '0', $t$ASK 645: a follow-up whose open words are the whole question is dropped$t$,
  $t$In run 42528 (odv1_question_round_log id 5) judge sol62's follow-up to the challenger named Q2 with open words "How does this passage fit Acts 2:30?", which is the whole of Q2's question. The engine passed it, so Q9 asked the same question again as a paid answer call. qfCheck accepted the open words when they stand word for word in the question or its passage; it tested that the words are found, not that they are a part. Change, the one statement in qfCheck in each of its three copies (QR Merge, QR Follow Build, QR Follow Final): one new fault when the normalized open words equal the normalized whole question, "the open words are the whole of Q<n>; a follow-up names the part its answer left open"; a faulted follow-up is DROPPED and recorded with its reply, as every faulted follow-up is. Expected effect: no paid answer call for a follow-up that repeats the whole question. The change reads ruling 515 as "a part". Not changed: the follow-up prompt, qfQuestion, the DROPPED handling, the answer call, ruling 515's wording, reasoning, a model setting, a token limit. The tighter form (open words only from the passage) is the operator's and is not in this row. (plan rev 0, header, heading 1 and 3, ask645/w4/plan645.md md5 be88af80)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 08:24 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12075; audit 42232), engine ebf1dbcf to 8470161f, on the 638 A fetch-back, and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12076: W1 built 638 A and then 645 on its own copy of 393bca2e and the result equals live 8470161f in all 426 nodes and the connections; t645 24 pass 0 fail; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL). QR Merge, QR Follow Build and QR Follow Final each gain one statement; nothing was deleted. IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. The written target is b3 (3edd747f), the build script unchanged from b1, rebuilt on the 638 A fetch-back. W1's recheck before the write (Wall 12072) named b2 (dbed99b4, on the 641 fetch-back) and ruled that no further grade was needed because 638 A does not touch the three QR nodes; after W3 asked, W1 compared the b3 target with the live engine it had read back and posted PASS on its md5 (Wall 12140: 426 of 426 node parameters and the connections equal). That check was made after the write. Offline (build b1 a47183fd, graded PASS by W1, Wall 12062): over the 24 follow-up checks stored in odv1_question_round_log rows 2 to 5, one changes, sol62's follow-up of Q2 in 42528, PASSED to DROPPED; the other three that name a question pass as before. W1's N1 on the plan (Wall 12056: the same question with its closing "?" left off would still pass) is met: trailing punctuation and spaces are set aside on both sides before the equality. NOT CHECKED by W1: the audit rows. Open: two clean live runs.$t$,
  '12050, 12056, 12058, 12062, 12069, 12072, 12075, 12076, 12121, 12128, 12129, 12140',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$W4's write card (cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58AtvDdVQtii3Ep8H2boYCMm, "Write ASK 645 (a follow-up that repeats the whole question is dropped)?"): he pressed "Write it" at 08:24 CST 2026-11-25. Card text, press and time are from W4's facts file; W3 did not read the card or the press. There was no build card: the build was offline files only, and the card came after the build grade.$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write it", "question": "Write ASK 645 (a follow-up that repeats the whole question is dropped)?", "options": {"Write it": "A follow-up whose open words are the whole question is dropped, with no paid answer call. Three Question Round nodes change.", "Hold": "Nothing is written; a judge can re-ask a whole question as a paid follow-up, as sol62 did in 42528."}, "thread": "W4", "card_id": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58AtvDdVQtii3Ep8H2boYCMm", "press_time": "08:24 CST 2026-11-25", "message_above_the_card": "cmsg_017ZQamDMHrS6fqMHnQDVo58AWdUc4gbGEcBse2HWfAYZS", "source": "W4's facts file aar/w3/cards_641_to_652_from_w4.md; W3 did not read the card or the press."}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "be88af8075cb59fd91a17ba2a70564a1", "path": "ask645/w4/plan645.md", "note": "plan rev 0, graded PASS WITH N1 by W1 (Wall 12056); N1 met in the build (Wall 12062).", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 12056"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"path": "ask645/w4/b3/b645.cjs", "md5": "a34629b2e0617e642ab08d2fc5b371fa", "what": "build script (the same file in b1 to b3)"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/b3/tg/target_engine_645.json", "md5": "3edd747fc160b53a6a2f85823337f123", "what": "target engine b3, on ebf1dbcf (written)"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/b2/tg/target_engine_645.json", "md5": "dbed99b43ed65461a47f84afdf1af8b4", "what": "target engine b2, on 393bca2e (not written)"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/b1/tg/target_engine_645.json", "md5": "a47183fdcd2e46d71497da621a11c2f7", "what": "target engine b1, on ee4e389d (not written)"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/b3/t645.cjs", "md5": "c82e941c10d8e89f5a2c949ef33ea5f7", "what": "test"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/write/atw/t645.txt", "md5": "d3a732879cb24b67ec0af2b3068c46b0", "what": "test output at the write"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/write/write645.sh", "md5": "2e5312b1ef666439e2df2e991854c2d9", "what": "write script"}, {"path": "ask645/w4/write/fetchback_eng_645.json", "md5": "cada8505b45e5117d9d2b1b2087c6e1c", "what": "fetch-back after the write"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"engine": "ask645/w4/write/revert_eng_645.json, md5 408d1f17c0261aa41a3d48c9ffa3c14e (restores ebf1dbcf)", "child": "not written; nothing to revert", "database": "not written; nothing to revert", "rehearsed": "not stated in the posts W3 read", "source": "Wall 12075; md5sum by W3"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS WITH N1 (plan rev 0)", "wall_id": 12056, "md5_graded": "be88af80", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12056"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (build b1)", "wall_id": 12062, "md5_graded": "a47183fd", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12062 (names \"build b1\"; the b1 target is a47183fd by Wall 12058)"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (recheck of b2 on live 393bca2e)", "wall_id": 12072, "md5_graded": "dbed99b4", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12072"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS (written target check of b3, made after the write: equal to the live 8470161f W1 read back, 426 of 426 node parameters and the connections)", "wall_id": 12140, "md5_graded": "3edd747fc160b53a6a2f85823337f123", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 12140"}]$j$::jsonb,
